{"task": "F1", "q": "Adaklu maize farmer planted late Feb, saw worms mid-March, sprayed the recommended chemicals with no effect. What next?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["chemical terms in question", "disease or pest terms in question", "no local reference for region 'adaklu' (coastal savannah zone; corpus covers Northern Ghana only for this question)"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": true, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": true, "problems": [], "figures_checked": 0, "sentences_checked": 3, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The farmer should scout the maize field at least once a week, looking for unusual patterns such as insect damage, larvae, or stunted growth [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "If the infestation persists despite spraying, consult your local Agricultural Extension Agent (AEA) for advice on recommended fall armyworm control pesticides in your area [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Additionally, consider rotating maize with non-host plants like groundnut, deep ploughing, and proper weeding to reduce future infestations [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}]}}]}, "draft": "Caution: the curated sources cover Northern Ghana only. The guidance below comes from them and may not apply in Adaklu; the officer should confirm local timing.\n\nThe farmer should scout the maize field at least once a week, looking for unusual patterns such as insect damage, larvae, or stunted growth [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting]. If the infestation persists despite spraying, consult your local Agricultural Extension Agent (AEA) for advice on recommended fall armyworm control pesticides in your area [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control]. Additionally, consider rotating maize with non-host plants like groundnut, deep ploughing, and proper weeding to reduce future infestations [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "drafted_by": "model", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 789, "completion_tokens": 152}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1946, "completion_tokens": 139}, "farmer_text": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 368, "completion_tokens": 77}}, "cost_usd": 0.000405}}
{"task": "F2", "q": "Is putting soil in the maize funnel enough to stop armyworm?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["disease or pest terms in question", "citation check failed: 'We do not know if this method is effective.' has no citation and is not supported by any cited passage (no shared content words)"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "stub(citation-check-fallback after llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct)", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": false, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'The passages do not mention this method.' is not supported by its citation ['APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention'] (no shared content words)", "'We do not know if putting soil in the maize funnel is enough to stop armyworm.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage lacks info"], "figures_checked": 0, "sentences_checked": 5, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "We do not know if putting soil in the maize funnel is enough to stop armyworm.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passage lacks info"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "To prevent Fall Armyworm, rotate maize with non-host plants like groundnut, deep plough and bury or burn infested maize residues, and weed maize fields properly [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "If infestations occur, consult your local Agricultural Extension Agent for advice on recommended pesticides [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Regularly scout the field for signs of infestation [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Implied by passage"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'We do not know if this method is effective.' has no citation and is not supported by any cited passage (no shared content words)"], "figures_checked": 0, "sentences_checked": 2, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The passages do not mention putting soil in the maize funnel as a method to stop armyworm [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "The passages do not mention putting soil in the maize funnel as a method to stop armyworm [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention]. We do not know if this method is effective."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"It is recommended to have a walk through the maize field at least once a week. When scouting, walk through the field and look out for unusual patterns such as insect damage on leaves, cobs or stems, presence of insect larvae or eggs on maize leaves, abnormal leaf colour, and stunted slow growing plants.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting]\n- \"Rotate maize with non-host plants such as groundnut to help reduce Fall Army worm infestations. Deep ploughing and burial, or burning of infested maize residues helps to reduce populations in the following season. Proper weeding of maize fields also helps to reduce infestations.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention]\n- \"Application of recommended pesticides can help to control infestations once they occur. Consult your local AEA for advice on the recommended fall army worm control pesticide in your area.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control]\nNote: Chemical use: AgriReach does not recommend products or doses. Refer to the label and the officer.\nNote: Possible pest/disease: this is not a diagnosis. Officer should inspect or refer.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1561, "completion_tokens": 205}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1115, "completion_tokens": 120}}, "cost_usd": 0.000392}}
