.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks]\n- \"At harvesting, maize grains are usually not fully dry and have a moisture content of about 15 to 20%. Immediately after harvesting, cobs should be dried so as to reduce the grain moisture content to about 10 to 12% in readiness for storage.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying]\n- \"Maize should be stored after removal of maize husks and shelling. Storing unhusked maize is not recommended as it is very difficult to detect insect infestations.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling]\nNote: Chemical use: AgriReach does not recommend products or doses. Refer to the label and the officer.\nNote: Possible pest/disease: this is not a diagnosis. Officer should inspect or refer.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1444, "completion_tokens": 267}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1318, "completion_tokens": 160}}, "cost_usd": 0.000431}}
{"task": "F7", "q": "Some of my stored maize is mouldy. Can I sell it or feed it to animals?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["food safety terms in question", "citation check failed: 'The officer should advise the farmer to check these limits before deciding whether to sel…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No advice given"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true], ["AGBETIAMEH-2018", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "stub(citation-check-fallback after llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct)", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": false, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'15 ppb' states 15 ppb as an upper limit, but the cited passage(s) ['AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits'] give(s) it as a plain value", "'If the levels exceed the limit, do not use it for food or feed.' is not supported by its citation ['APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying'] (no shared content words)", "'Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No direct claim", "'Test the maize for aflatoxin levels before deciding.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No test mentioned", "'Proper storage is crucial to prevent mould.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No mould mentioned"], "figures_checked": 3, "sentences_checked": 8, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No direct claim"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Mould can indicate aflatoxin contamination, which has strict limits.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Aflatoxin limits"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The Ghana Standards Authority allows up to 15 ppb aflatoxin in maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "GSA limit"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Test the maize for aflatoxin levels before deciding.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No test mentioned"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "Proper storage is crucial to prevent mould.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No mould mentioned"}, {"n": 6, "sentence": "Ensure maize is well dried (10-12% moisture) and shelled before storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Moisture content"}, {"n": 7, "sentence": "Use recommended storage chemicals and appropriate containers [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Storage chemicals"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'The officer should advise the farmer to check these limits before deciding whether to sel…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No advice given"], "figures_checked": 3, "sentences_checked": 3, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which have limits set by different authorities: the European Union at 4 ppb, the Ghana Standards Authority at 15 ppb for maize, and the United States Food and Drugs Administration at 20 ppb [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "The officer should advise the farmer to check these limits before deciding whether to sell or feed the maize.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No advice given"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Proper storage is important to prevent mould, but the passages do not provide specific advice on what to do with already mouldy maize.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage silent"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which have limits set by different authorities: the European Union at 4 ppb, the Ghana Standards Authority at 15 ppb for maize, and the United States Food and Drugs Administration at 20 ppb [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]. The officer should advise the farmer to check these limits before deciding whether to sell or feed the maize. Proper storage is important to prevent mould, but the passages do not provide specific advice on what to do with already mouldy maize."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Maize should be stored after removal of maize husks and shelling. Storing unhusked maize is not recommended as it is very difficult to detect insect infestations.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling]\n- \"Well dried and shelled maize should be treated with recommended storage chemicals and stored in jute sacks lined with polythene bags.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks]\n- \"At harvesting, maize grains are usually not fully dry and have a moisture content of about 15 to 20%. Immediately after harvesting, cobs should be dried so as to reduce the grain moisture content to about 10 to 12% in readiness for storage.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying]\n- \"aflatoxin limits imposed by the European Union (4 ppb), the Ghana Standards Authority (GSA; 15 ppb for maize and 20 ppb for groundnut), and the United States Food and Drugs Administration (FDA; 20 ppb)\" [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]\nNote: Chemical use: AgriReach does not recommend products or doses. Refer to the label and the officer.\nNote: Possible food-safety risk (mould/aflatoxin): AgriReach cannot clear produce for sale, food or feed. Officer should advise.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1772, "completion_tokens": 283}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1535, "completion_tokens": 232}}, "cost_usd": 0.000417}}
